      "lineNbr": 480,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-03T02:39:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "on entry this points at the max size of the response buffer, you be checking that this is not exceeded at any point.\n\nAlso, to add insult to injury this value is going to be around 2K, but if the command arrives over USB, max it can send back is one USB chunk, i.e. 64 bytes less header size, in fact both rx and tx can not exceed 64 bytes less header size, as there is no segmentation/reassembly.\n\nThis all is very brittle, you should make sure that all your data fits into 64 less header size both in and out.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 480,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 480,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "c9281f995a64352a74c25574d026dd6df94aa997",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
